---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { company } from '../data/site';
const c = company.contact;
---
<Legal title="Terms and Conditions" path="/terms" updated="27 November 2026"
  description="The terms that apply when you use findoursmart.com or buy services from SMART (Pvt) Ltd, including quotes, payments, delivery and support.">
  <p>These terms apply when you use findoursmart.com or buy services from {company.legalName} ("SMART", "we", "us"). By asking us to start work, you agree to them. If a written quote or agreement for your project says something different, that document applies to your project.</p>

  <h2>Quotes and prices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Prices on this site are in Sri Lankan Rupees (LKR) and are shown as ranges. Where your project falls in the range depends on what you need.</li>
    <li>Before we start, we send a quote with the scope, the exact price and the delivery time. The price in that quote is fixed for the scope it describes.</li>
    <li>Work outside the agreed scope is quoted separately before we do it.</li>
    <li>Third-party costs, such as advertising budgets, paid plugins, SMS or WhatsApp Business API charges, are not included unless the quote says so.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Small packages are paid in advance or as stated in the quote. Larger projects are split into milestones.</li>
    <li>Monthly plans are billed in advance and continue until cancelled.</li>
    <li>We may pause work or services when an invoice is overdue.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Delivery</h2>
  <p>Delivery times start when we have received payment and everything we need from you, such as text, photos and logins. Delays in receiving these move the delivery date.</p>

  <h2>Changes and approval</h2>
  <p>We share previews while we work. Each package includes reasonable rounds of changes within the agreed scope. Once you approve the final version, further changes are new work.</p>

  <h2>Domains and hosting</h2>
  <p>Where a package includes a domain and hosting, they are included for the period stated. After that, they renew at the rate we tell you in advance. If renewal is not paid, the domain and site may go offline.</p>

  <h2>Ownership</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Once paid in full, you own the content and design we create specifically for you. Domains we register for you are in your name.</li>
    <li>We keep ownership of our own tools, templates and reusable code, and give you a licence to use them as part of your project.</li>
    <li>Our products, including KadaBook, are licensed under their own terms and are not transferred to you.</li>
    <li>We may show your project in our portfolio unless you ask us not to.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your content</h2>
  <p>You confirm you have the right to use any text, images, logos and other material you give us, and that it does not break any law.</p>

  <h2>Support</h2>
  <p>We fix faults in our work that you report within 30 days of launch at no charge. Support after that is provided under a support plan or charged per request.</p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>We do our work with care and skill. To the extent the law allows, we are not responsible for indirect losses such as lost profit, and our total liability for a project is limited to the amount you paid for it.</p>

  <h2>Cancellation</h2>
  <p>You can cancel a project at any time. Work completed up to that point is charged. Monthly plans can be cancelled with notice before the next billing date.</p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka, and disputes fall under the jurisdiction of the courts of Sri Lanka.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>{company.legalName}<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${c.email}`}>{c.email}</a><br />
    Phone and WhatsApp: <a href={`tel:${c.phone}`}>{c.phoneDisplay}</a><br />
    {[c.address, c.city, c.postalCode, c.country].filter(Boolean).join(', ')}
  </p>
</Legal>
